00:14:42,857 --> 00:14:48,857
As Australian cinema broke through to international audiences in the 1970s through respected art house films like Peter Weir's "Picnic At
Hanging Rock," a new underground of low-budget exploitation filmmakers were turning out considerably less highbrow fare.

4
00:19:37,142 --> 00:19:43,142
Documentary filmmaker Mark Hartley explores this unbridled era of sex and violence, complete with clips from
some of the scene's most outrageous flicks and interviews with the renegade filmmakers themselves.

